# Local iOS IPA package

Produce a local iOS `.ipa` package for sideloading and testing without App Store
submission or an Xcode-dependent authoring workflow. Keep every unavoidable
Apple signing, SDK, entitlement, or build-host constraint explicit.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Offer iOS ARM64 as one selectable target in
  `tools/build/adapter-inbound/arch.py`.
- [ ] Publish the successful native deliverable as an IPA beneath the canonical
  `dist/` architecture output.
- [ ] Do not add App Store submission, review, notarization, or installation
  tutorial steps to the supported SHAR workflow.
- [ ] Do not require Xcode as an authoring UI; if Unreal or Apple tooling still
  requires Apple SDK, signing, or a macOS build host, detect and report that
  requirement instead of pretending the build is host-independent.
- [ ] Keep signing inputs, temporary provisioning material, cook/staging output,
  and logs outside the final IPA and under declared local build state.

## Dependencies

Depends on the canonical multi-platform build runner and its validated external
platform prerequisites.

## Native Unreal asset pivot — 2026-09-12

Normalized extracted JSON and versioned normalized plans are the canonical
production handoff into Unreal. FBX is deprecated for production Unreal asset
construction and may remain only as temporary interoperability, inspection, or
migration evidence. New implementation work must construct target assets
through tested native Unreal automation without making FBX transforms, scene
units, material slots, or importer behavior authoritative. Existing FBX-based
evidence remains historical or transitional and must be retired from production
once the equivalent native constructor has parity coverage.

